  history: Dixmude was a Zeppelin built for the Imperial German Navy as L 72 (LZ
    114) and unfinished at the end of the First World War, when it was given to France
    as war reparations and recommissioned for service in the French Navy. On 21 December
    1923 it was lost during a thunderstorm over Mediterranean, killing everyone onboard.
